      ":question/id": "4a81fec4-e469-52d1-b3ae-2d2d1e2bd280",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-1-(2)xy?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(3,-2)$,$(2,-2)$,$(0,-2)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,-2)}=-1-2(3)(-2)=11, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=-1-2(2)(-2)=7, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-2)}=-1-2(0)(-2)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/da/da38e55a37f775b3e531b61436ff070901cd88f7ce4a7c9229f096e87159c3c8.png)"
